# CPENT Challenge 108 – Identify Rsync Shared Directory

## Challenge

**Question:**

> Identify the shared directory accessible via the Rsync service running on the machine located at `192.168.1.136`.

**Target:**

```text
192.168.1.136
```

**Answer Format:**

```text
Xxxxx
```

**Final Answer:**

```text
James
```

---

## Step 1 – Identify the Rsync Service

Rsync normally runs on TCP port **873**.

We scanned port 873 and used the Rsync enumeration script:

```bash
nmap -p 873 --script rsync-list-modules 192.168.1.136
```

### Output

```text
PORT    STATE SERVICE
873/tcp open  rsync
```

This confirmed that an **Rsync service** was running on the target.

However, Nmap did not display the available Rsync module/share name.

---

## Step 2 – Enumerate Rsync Shares

We queried the Rsync service directly:

```bash
rsync rsync://192.168.1.136/
```

### Output

```text
James           Entire james account backup
```

The first column is the **Rsync module/share name**.

Therefore:

```text
James
```

is the shared directory/module accessible through Rsync.

---

## Step 3 – Match the Answer Format

The challenge requires:

```text
Xxxxx
```

The discovered share is:

```text
James
```

It matches the required format.

